Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by a mismatch between the display of subtest indices (which were changed to start from 1 for user-friendly output) and the actual invocation of subtests, which relied on zero-based indexing. This led to the incorrect subtest being executed, as the second subtest in the array was invoked instead of the first, resulting in failures for certain tests.

